{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DeBFCXhkY1NxWdcysTzTac","type":"tool_result","content":"/-- If the support of the simple graph `G` is a subset of the set `s`, then the induced subgraph of\n`s` has the same number of edges as `G`. -/\ntheorem card_edgeFinset_induce_of_support_subset (h : G.support ⊆ s) :\n    #(G.induce s).edgeFinset = #G.edgeFinset := by\n  rw [← map_edgeFinset_induce_of_support_subset h, card_map]\n\ntheorem card_edgeFinset_induce_support :\n    #(G.induce G.support).edgeFinset = #G.edgeFinset :=\n  card_edgeFinset_induce_of_support_subset subset_rfl\n\ntheorem map_neighborFinset_induce [DecidableEq V] (v : s) :\n    ((G.induce s).neighborFinset v).map (.subtype (· ∈ s)) = G.neighborFinset v ∩ s.toFinset := by\n  ext; simp\n\ntheorem map_neighborFinset_induce_of_neighborSet_subset {v : s} (h : G.neighborSet v ⊆ s) :\n    ((G.induce s).neighborFinset v).map (.subtype (· ∈ s)) = G.neighborFinset v := by\n  classical\n  rwa [← Set.toFinset_subset_toFinset, ← neighborFinset_def, ← inter_eq_left,\n    ← map_neighborFinset_induce v] at h\n\n/-- If the neighbor set of a vertex `v` is a subset of `s`, then the degree of the vertex in the\ninduced subgraph of `s` is the same as in `G`. -/\ntheorem degree_induce_of_neighborSet_subset {v : s} (h : G.neighborSet v ⊆ s) :\n    (G.induce s).degree v = G.degree v := by\n  simp_rw [← card_neighborFinset_eq_degree,\n    ← map_neighborFinset_induce_of_neighborSet_subset h, card_map]\n\n/-- If the support of the simple graph `G` is a subset of the set `s`, then the degree of vertices\nin the induced subgraph of `s` are the same as in `G`. -/\ntheorem degree_induce_of_support_subset (h : G.support ⊆ s) (v : s) :\n    (G.induce s).degree v = G.degree v :=\n\"\"\"The statements of `lean/MOSPFormalization/Minor.lean`, checked on small graphs.\n\nLean models a contraction on a fixed vertex type: `contractEdge G u v` merges\n`v` into `u` (u keeps its label, as in `pathwidth_solver/pathwidth/minor.py`)\nand leaves `v` as an isolated vertex; a deletion step removes every edge at\n`v`; the minor is the graph induced on the vertices never removed. Checked\nhere, with the subset DP as the oracle:\n\n* that model, induced on the alive vertices, is exactly the code's `replay`;\n* `pw(contractEdge G u v) <= pw(G)` for every edge `uv`, on the full vertex\n  type with `v` isolated (the one-step Lean statement);\n* `pw(minor) <= pw(G)` for random valid sequences, contractions and deletions\n  mixed, not only the greedy ones `test_minor_bound.py` checks;\n* a control: identifying two *non-adjacent* vertices can raise the pathwidth,\n  so the edge hypothesis of the Lean theorem is not decorative.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport random\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport networkx as nx\n\nfrom fixed_parameter_algorithm.pathwidth import compute_pathwidth\n\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\nsys.path.insert(0, str(ROOT / \"pathwidth_solver\"))\nfrom pathwidth.minor import replay  # noqa: E402\n\n\ndef pw(adj, vertices):\n    G = nx.Graph()\n    G.add_nodes_from(vertices)\n    for x in vertices:\n        for y in adj[x]:\n            if y in vertices:\n                G.add_edge(x, y)\n    return compute_pathwidth(G)[0] if G.number_of_nodes() else 0\n\n\ndef contract_edge(adj, u, v):\n    \"\"\"Lean's `contractEdge G u v`: Adj x y iff x != y, x, y != v and\n    (G.Adj x y or x = u and G.Adj v y or y = u and G.Adj v x).\"\"\"\n    n = len(adj)\n    out = [set() for _ in range(n)]\n    for x in range(n):\n        for y in range(n):\n            if x != y and x != v and y != v and (\n                    y in adj[x] or (x == u and y in adj[v]) or (y == u and x in adj[v])):\n                out[x].add(y)\n    return out\n\n\ndef delete_vertex(adj, v):\n    \"\"\"Lean's `isolate G v`: Adj x y iff G.Adj x y and x, y != v.\"\"\"\n    return [set() if x == v else {y for y in s if y != v} for x, s in enumerate(adj)]\n\n\ndef random_graph(rng, n):\n    p = rng.uniform(0.15, 0.7)\npaper1/latex/main.tex:49:% appendix, \\leanentry{key}{result} opens a row and \\leannames{a, b} prints the\npaper1/latex/main.tex:53:\\newcommand{\\leannames}[1]{\\def\\lean@sep{}\\@for\\lean@n:=#1\\do{\\lean@sep\\expandafter\\path\\expandafter{\\lean@n}\\def\\lean@sep{, }}}\npaper1/latex/main.tex:55:\\newcounter{leanentry}\npaper1/latex/main.tex:56:\\renewcommand{\\theleanentry}{A.\\arabic{leanentry}}\npaper1/latex/main.tex:57:\\newcommand{\\leanentry}[2]{\\leavevmode\\refstepcounter{leanentry}\\label{lean:#1}\\theleanentry & #2 &}\n    \"MOSPInstance.treewidth_add_one_le_mospValue\",\n    \"pathwidth_bot_fin4\",\n    \"old_branch_statement_false\",\n    # loop0004 item 13: the separator form of the branch lemma (Lemma A of §38).\n    \"PathDecomposition.middle_bag_false_linked\",\n    \"branch_lemma_linked\",\n    \"branch_lemma_separator\",\n    \"branch_lemma_separator_treewidth\",\n    \"induce_singleton_connected\",\n    \"branch_lemma_of_separator\",\n    # item 09's fitted conjecture, proved on 2026-10-31 as a corollary of `tw ≤ pw`\n    # and Harper's `f(6) ≤ pw + 6`, so promoted from STATED (loop0010 item 01's gate)\n    \"conjecture_sqrt_tw_f6\",\n)\n#: loop0010 item 11, `lean/MOSPFormalization/ForestCover.lean`: the blow-up bound\n#: `mospValue ≤ ω (pathwidth (incidence) + 1)` for every instance, its forest form\n#: through `TreeBound.lean`, subinstance monotonicity, and the coupling inclusion\n#: of item 10 (Lemma V2) over `CliqueCoverMoment.lean`'s covers, and the layer\n#: lemma of item 07 (Lemma L: a layering `lvl` gives `pathwidth ≤ max (|L_i| + |L_{i+1}|) − 1`).\nFOREST_COVER_PROVED = (\n    \"PathDecomposition.mem_bag_of_meet\",\n    \"isEmptyPair_anti\",\n    \"MOSPInstance.incidence\",\n    \"MOSPInstance.one_le_maxPatternSize_iff\",\n    \"MOSPInstance.blowUp\",\n    \"MOSPInstance.blowUp_width_add_one_le\",\n    \"MOSPInstance.pathwidth_mospGraph_add_one_le\",\n    \"MOSPInstance.mospValue_le_maxPatternSize_mul\",\n    \"le_treeBound_treeBoundInv\",\n    \"treeBound_lt_of_lt_treeBoundInv\",\n    \"pathwidth_le_treeBoundInv_of_isAcyclic\",\n    \"MOSPInstance.mospValue_le_of_incidence_isAcyclic\",\n    \"MOSPInstance.mospGraph_mono\",\n    \"MOSPInstance.mospValue_mono\",\n    \"coverGraph_mono\",\n    \"isEmptyPair_coverGraph_of_subset\",\n    \"pathwidth_coverGraph_mono\",\n    # the layer lemma of item 07 (Lemma L), pathwidth and vertex-separation forms\n    \"layerDecomposition\",\n    \"pathwidth_le_layerWidth\",\n    \"vertexSeparation_le_layerWidth\",\n    \"isLayering_dist\",\n    \"pathwidth_le_layerWidth_dist\",\n)\n#: loop0010 item 13 (`PendantCliques.lean`): Lemma P, the two-sided pendant bound, §6.5 (L5).\nPENDANT_PROVED = (\n    \"PathDecomposition.pendant_bound\",\n    \"pathwidth_ge_of_pendant_cliques\",\n    \"pathwidth_ge_of_clique_pendant_cliques\",\n    \"MOSPInstance.mospValue_ge_of_pendant_patterns\",\n)\n#: loop0011 item 10 (`SeparatorMoment.lean`): counting events, not witnesses —\n#: L1 (the balanced separator at exact sizes) and its cover form, L1′ (the pair\n#: form of `E_bip`, the connectivity step, the relaxed event, the `3K₂` example),\n#: L2 (the Galois step, the one-round closure, the closed pair), Lemma W (the\n#: weighted-count identity), the union bound over separators, the factorisation\n#: step, the relabelling, Theorem S with its `n.choose k` factor, the union bound\n#: of Theorem Cl, Lemma Fl (the flips) and Corollary W-flip's sound part; since\n#: item 13 the product over blocks and Theorem Cl's independence step too.\nSEPARATOR_PROVED = (\n    \"exists_balanced_separator\",","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"171ae345-0826-42fc-976d-fc244650ed98","uuid":"072a1416-1205-46d9-bceb-9664375569e6","timestamp":"2026-11-03T10:12:19.095Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"/-- If the support of the simple graph `G` is a subset of the set `s`, then the induced subgraph of\n`s` has the same number of edges as `G`. -/\ntheorem card_edgeFi