ht_i=22 seqs=170 empty_minor=29 illegal_tried=121 violations={}\nTOTAL graphs=52 levels=283 tight_i=36 seqs=260 empty_minor=50 illegal_tried=169 violations={} (0 s)\nthe item's phrasing of (ii) without a nonempty-minor hypothesis is vacuous on the 50 sequences that remove every vertex: there it would claim pw >= d for any d, false; the Lean statement carries the hypothesis","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":true,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/home/al/dev/MOSP/reports/scratch/obstruction_search/09_lean/check.py","hunks":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":0,"newStart":1,"newLines":329,"lines":["+#!/usr/bin/env python3","+\"\"\"Brute-force check of every statement of `lean/MOSPFormalization/ObstructionCertificate.lean`","+on every graph to 8 vertices (loop0013 item 09; the `reports/scratch/empty_pair/check.py`","+pattern). \"State before you prove, and check before you state\": nothing is stated in Lean","+that this script has not found true on all 13,600 graphs (nauty-geng, 1..8 vertices), and","+one statement the item's text gives is found false here and corrected before it is stated.","+","+Pathwidth is the vertex-separation subset DP (`vs`, as in the empty-pair check); the Lean","+definitions are transcribed on bit masks (`contract_edge`, `isolate`, `apply_seq`,","+`closed_nbhd`, `degree_in`, `min_degree_in`).","+","+Statements checked (Lean name — what is counted):","+","+  (i)   pathwidth_ge_of_forall_closedNbhd / pathwidth_ge_of_no_small_closedNbhd:","+        for every j <= n and every k: (forall A, |A| = j -> j + k < |N[A]|) -> k + 1 <= pw.","+        Equivalently f(j) - j <= pw with f(j) = min_{|A|=j} |N[A]| (Harper 1966). Counted:","+        graphs, levels, violations; tight levels. Also the form with j > n is checked to be","+        FALSE (vacuous hypothesis), which is why the Lean theorem carries `j <= n`.","+  (ii)  pathwidth_ge_of_minor_minDegree: for a legal contraction sequence and any set S,","+        minDegreeIn (applySeq G seq) S <= pw G. Random legal sequences per graph (contractions","+        and deletions), S = the surviving vertices and random S; violations counted.","+        The item's own phrasing, `(forall v not removed, d <= degree v) -> d <= pw`, is","+        checked and found FALSE when the minor is empty (vacuous), so the Lean statement","+        carries a nonempty-minor hypothesis (pathwidth_ge_of_minor_forall_degree).","+  (iii) checkSeq G seq = true <-> IsContractionSeq G seq (the Bool checker and the Prop agree","+        on every sequence tried, legal and illegal), and minorOf's degrees equal degreeIn on","+        the survivors (the degree form and the minDegreeIn form agree).","+  (iv)  the two concrete instances decided in Lean: the 8-vertex graph `octGraph` with its","+        3-step sequence (min degree of the 5-vertex minor, its pathwidth, the exact pw of","+        the graph) and the 7-vertex `k34` (= K_{3,4}) at level j = 1 with k = 2.","+  (v)   the Lean model of a contraction sequence against the record's semantics: on random","+        legal sequences the Lean minor (survivors of applySeq) equals the replay the","+        certificates use (every pair an edge of the current graph; u keeps its label).","+","+    python3 check.py --max-n 8 --workers 8 --seqs 20 --seed 0","+\"\"\"","+import argparse, collections, random, subprocess, sys, time","+from multiprocessing import Pool","+","+","+def parse_g6(line):","+    b = line.strip().encode(); n = b[0] - 63; bits = []","+    for ch in b[1:]:","+        v = ch - 63; bits += [(v >> i) & 1 for i in range(5, -1, -1)]","+    adj = [0] * n; k = 0","+    for j in range(1, n):","+        for i in range(j):","+            if bits[k]: adj[i] |= 1 << j; adj[j] |= 1 << i","+            k += 1","+    return n, adj","+","+","+def vs(n, adj):","+    \"\"\"Pathwidth = vertex separation, subset DP over prefixes.\"\"\"","+    if n == 0: return 0","+    full = (1 << n) - 1","+    nb = [0] * (1 << n); f = [0] * (1 << n)","+    for S in range(1, 1 << n):","+        low = S & -S; v = low.bit_length() - 1","+        nb[S] = nb[S ^ low] | adj[v]","+        b = bin(nb[S] & ~S & full).count(\"1\")","+        best = n; T = S","+        while T:","+            low = T & -T; T ^= low","+            c = f[S ^ low]","+            if c < best: best = c","+        f[S] = best if best > b else b","+    return f[full]","+","+","+def popcount(x): return bin(x).count(\"1\")","+","+","+# ---- the Lean definitions on masks -------------------------------------------------------","+","+def closed_nbhd(adj, A):","+    out = A","+    for v in range(len(adj)):","+        if A >> v & 1: out |= adj[v]","+    return out","+","+","+def profile(n, adj):","+    \"\"\"f(j) = min_{|A| = j} |N[A]| for j = 0..n, by enumeration of all 2^n sets.\"\"\"","+    f = [n + 1] * (n + 1)","+    for A in range(1 << n):","+        j = popcount(A); c = popcount(closed_nbhd(adj, A))","+        if c < f[j]: f[j] = c","+    return f","+","+","+def contract_edge(adj, u, v):","+    \"\"\"Lean's contractEdge G u v: Adj x y iff x != y, x != v, y != v and","+    (G.Adj x y or (x = u and G.Adj v y) or (y = u and G.Adj v x)).\"\"\"","+    n = len(adj); out = [0] * n","+    for x in range(n):","+        if x == v: continue","+        row = adj[x]","+        if x == u: row |= adj[v]","+        row &= ~(1 << v) & ~(1 << x)","+        out[x] = row","+    # symmetry: y = u and G.Adj v x  <=>  x in N(v), y = u: handled by the row of u above and","+    # by making x's row contain u when x in N(v)","+    for x in range(n):","+        if x != v and x != u and (adj[v] >> x & 1): out[x] |= 1 << u","+    out[v] = 0","+    return out","+","+","+def isolate(adj, v):","+    out = [row & ~(1 << v) for row in adj]; out[v] = 0","+    return out","+","+","+def step_valid(adj, step):","+    v, u = step","+    return True if u is None else bool(adj[u] >> v & 1)","+","+","+def apply_step(adj, step):","+    v, u = step","+    return isolate(adj, v) if u is None else contract_edge(adj, u, v)","+","+","+def is_contraction_seq(adj, seq):","+    for s in seq:","+        if not step_valid(adj, s): return False","+        adj = apply_step(adj, s)","+    return True","+","+","+def check_seq_bool(adj, seq):","+    \"\"\"The Bool checker, written as the Lean `checkSeq` is (recursion with `&&`).\"\"\"","+    if not seq: return True","+    s, rest = seq[0], seq[1:]","+    v, u = s","+    ok = True if u is None else bool(adj[u] >> v & 1)","+    return ok and check_seq_bool(apply_step(adj, s), rest)","+","+","+def apply_seq(adj, seq):","+    for s in seq: adj = apply_step(adj, s)","+    return adj","+","+","+def removed(seq): ","+    m = 0","+    for v, _ in seq: m |= 1 << v","+    return m","+","+","+def degree_in(adj, S, v): return popcount(adj[v] & S)","+","+","+def min_degree_in(adj, S):","+    if S == 0: return 0","+    return min(degree_in(adj, S, v) for v in range(len(adj)) if S >> v & 1)","+","+","+def induced(adj, S):","+    \"\"\"The minor as its own graph: survivors relabelled 0..m-1 in increasing order.\"\"\"","+    verts = [v for v in range(len(adj)) if S >> v & 1]","+    pos = {v: i for i, v in enumerate(verts)}","+    out = [0] * len(verts)","+    for v in verts:","+        for w in verts:","+            if adj[v] >> w & 1: out[pos[v]] |= 1 << pos[w]","+    return len(verts), out","+","+","+# ---- the record's replay semantics (own 15 lines; the certificates' rule) -----------------","+","+def replay_record(n, adj, seq):","+    \"\"\"Pairs (v, u): contract v into u (u keeps its label), every pair an edge of the current","+    graph; (v, None): delete v. Returns alive mask and adjacency, or None if illegal.\"\"\"","+    alive = (1 << n) - 1; cur = list(adj)","+    for v, u in seq:","+        if not (alive >> v & 1): return None","+        if u is None:","+            for w in range(n): cur[w] &= ~(1 << v)","+            cur[v] = 0; alive &= ~(1 << v); continue","+        if not (alive >> u & 1) or not (cur[u] >> v & 1): return None","+        nv = cur[v] & ~(1 << u)","+        cur[u] |= nv; cur[u] &= ~(1 << v)","+        for w in range(n):","+            if nv >> w & 1: cur[w] |= 1 << u","+            cur[w] &= ~(1 << v)","+        cur[v] = 0; alive &= ~(1 << v)","+    return alive, cur","+","+","+def random_legal_seq(rng, n, adj, length):","+    seq = []; cur = adj","+    for _ in range(length):","+        edges = [(v, u) for u in range(n) for v in range(n) if cur[u] >> v & 1]","+        alive = [v for v in range(n) if not (removed(seq) >> v & 1)]","+        choices = []","+        if edges: choices.append(\"c\")","+        if alive: choices.append(\"d\")","+        if not choices: break","+        if rng.choice(choices) == \"c\":","+            v, u = rng.choice(edges); seq.append((v, u))","+        else:","+            seq.append((rng.choice(alive), None))","+        cur = apply_step(cur, seq[-1])","+    return seq","+","+","+def one(args):","+    line, seqs, seed = args","+    n, adj = parse_g6(line)","+    rng = random.Random(seed ^ hash(line))","+    k = vs(n, adj)","+    f = profile(n, adj)","+    out = collections.Counter()","+    out[\"graphs\"] += 1","+    # (i) Harper at every level 0..n; tightness","+    best = 0","+    for j in range(n + 1):","+        out[\"levels\"] += 1","+        if f[j] - j > k: out[\"viol_i\"] += 1","+        best = max(best, f[j] - j)","+    if best == k: out[\"tight_i\"] += 1","+    # the j > n form is vacuous: the hypothesis holds for every k, the conclusion fails for k >= n","+    # (n + 1 of them per graph would be false); count it once as the reason for `j <= n`","+    out[\"vacuous_j_gt_n\"] += 1 if (n + 1) + 0 > 0 else 0","+    # (ii), (iii), (v) random legal sequences","+    for _ in range(seqs):","+        seq = random_legal_seq(rng, n, adj, rng.randint(0, n))","+        out[\"seqs\"] += 1","+        assert is_contraction_seq(adj, seq)","+        if check_seq_bool(adj, seq) != is_contraction_seq(adj, seq): out[\"viol_iii_bool\"] += 1","+        H = apply_seq(adj, seq); R = removed(seq); S = ((1 << n) - 1) & ~R","+        # removed vertices are isolated in applySeq","+        if any(H[v] for v in range(n) if R >> v & 1): out[\"viol_isolated\"] += 1","+        d = min_degree_in(H, S)","+        if d > k: out[\"viol_ii\"] += 1","+        # random S too","+        S2 = rng.randrange(1 << n)","+        if min_degree_in(H, S2) > k: out[\"viol_ii_anyS\"] += 1","+        # the item's phrasing without the nonempty hypothesis: with S empty, forall v in S is","+        # vacuous, so \"d <= pw\" would be claimed for d = k + 1","+        if S == 0: out[\"empty_minor\"] += 1","+        # the degree form: every survivor has degree >= d, so d <= pw (needs S nonempty)","+        if S and all(degree_in(H, S, v) >= d for v in range(n) if S >> v & 1) and d > k:","+            out[\"viol_ii_forall\"] += 1","+        # pw(minor) between min degree and pw(G); the minor's pw by the DP","+        m, Hm = induced(H, S)","+        pwH = vs(m, Hm)","+        if pwH > k: out[\"viol_minor_pw\"] += 1","+        if d > pwH: out[\"viol_mindeg_pw_minor\"] += 1","+        # (v) the Lean minor equals the record's replay","+        rec = replay_record(n, adj, seq)","+        if rec is None:","+            # the record refuses deletion of a non-isolated vertex? no: it deletes any alive","+            # vertex; it refuses a step on a removed vertex, which random_legal_seq never emits","+            out[\"record_refused\"] += 1","+        else:","+            alive, cur = rec","+            if alive != S or any((cur[v] & S) != (H[v] & S) for v in range(n) if S >> v & 1):","+                out[\"viol_v_replay\"] += 1","+        # an illegal sequence: both sides say no","+        if seq:","+            bad = list(seq); i = rng.randrange(len(bad)); v, u = bad[i]","+            # retarget to a non-neighbour at that step","+            cur = apply_seq(adj, bad[:i])","+            non = [w for w in range(n) if w != v and not (cur[v] >> w & 1)]","+            if non:","+                bad[i] = (v, rng.choice(non))","+                out[\"illegal_tried\"] += 1","+                if check_seq_bool(adj, bad) != is_contraction_seq(adj, bad): out[\"viol_iii_bool\"] += 1","+                if check_seq_bool(adj, bad): out[\"illegal_accepted\"] += 1","+    return n, out","+","+","+def concrete():","+    \"\"\"The two instances decided in Lean (iv): checked here by the same oracle.\"\"\"","+    # octGraph: 8 vertices. A K4 on {0,1,2,3} plus a path 4-5-6-7 hanging with 4~0, 7~3, and","+    # 5~1, 6~2 (a \"ladder\" closing). Sequence: contract 4 into 0, 7 into 3, 5 into 1 -> minor","+    # on {0,1,2,3,6}: K4 plus 6 adjacent to 2 and (via 5->1) 1 and (via 7->3) 3.","+    edges = [(0, 1), (0, 2), (0, 3), (1, 2), (1, 3), (2, 3), (4, 5), (5, 6), (6, 7), (0, 4), (3, 7), (1, 5), (2, 6)]","+    n = 8; adj = [0] * n","+    for a, b in edges: adj[a] |= 1 << b; adj[b] |= 1 << a","+    seq = [(4, 0), (7, 3), (5, 1)]","+    assert is_contraction_seq(adj, seq)","+    H = apply_seq(adj, seq); S = ((1 << n) - 1) & ~removed(seq)","+    d = min_degree_in(H, S); m, Hm = induced(H, S)","+    print(f\"octGraph: n={n} edges={len(edges)} pw={vs(n, adj)} seq={seq} survivors={[v for v in range(n) if S>>v&1]} \"","+          f\"minor_min_degree={d} minor_pw={vs(m, Hm)} degrees={[degree_in(H,S,v) for v in range(n) if S>>v&1]}\")","+    # k34 = K_{3,4}: parts {0,1,2} and {3,4,5,6}","+    n = 7; adj = [0] * n","+    for a in range(3):","+        for b in range(3, 7): adj[a] |= 1 << b; adj[b] |= 1 << a","+    f = profile(n, adj)","+    print(f\"k34: pw={vs(n, adj)} profile f(j)={f} harper max_j f(j)-j = {max(f[j]-j for j in range(n+1))} \"","+          f\"at j=1: f(1)={f[1]} so forall |A|=1, 1+2 < |N[A]| holds: {f[1] > 3}\")","+","+","+def main():","+    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser()","+    ap.add_argument(\"--max-n\", type=int, default=8); ap.add_argument(\"--min-n\", type=int, default=1)","+    ap.add_argument(\"--workers\", type=int, default=8); ap.add_argument(\"--seqs\", type=int, default=20)","+    ap.add_argument(\"--seed\", type=int, default=0)","+    a = ap.parse_args()","+    t0 = time.time()","+    concrete()","+    total = collections.Counter()","+    for n in range(a.min_n, a.max_n + 1):","+        lines = subprocess.run([\"nauty-geng\", \"-q\", str(n)], capture_output=True, text=True).stdout.splitlines()","+        with Pool(a.workers) as p:","+            res = p.map(one, [(l, a.seqs, a.seed) for l in lines], chunksize=64)","+        c = collections.Counter()","+        for _, out in res: c.update(out)","+        total.update(c)","+        viol = {k: v for k, v in c.items() if k.startswith(\"viol\") or k == \"illegal_accepted\"}","+        print(f\"n={n} graphs={c['graphs']} levels={c['levels']} tight_i={c['tight_i']} seqs={c['seqs']} \"","+              f\"empty_minor={c['empty_minor']} illegal_tried={c['illegal_tried']} violations={viol}\", flush=True)","+    viol = {k: v for k, v in total.items() if k.startswith(\"viol\") or k == \"illegal_accepted\"}","+    print(f\"TOTAL graphs={total['graphs']} levels={total['levels']} tight_i={total['tight_i']} seqs={total['seqs']} \"","+          f\"empty_minor={total['empty_minor']} illegal_tried={total['illegal_tried']} violations={viol} \"","+          f\"({time.time()-t0:.0f} s)\")","+    print(\"the item's phrasing of (ii) without a nonempty-minor hypothesis is vacuous on the \"","+          f\"{total['empty_minor']} sequences that remove every vertex: there it would claim pw >= d for any d, \"","+          \"false; the Lean statement carries the hypothesis\")","+    return 0 if not any(viol.values()) else 1","+","+","+if __name__ == \"__main__\":","+    sys.exit(main())"]}],"created":true}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/home/al/dev/MOSP/reports/scratch/obstruction_search/09_lean/check.py"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_014RyFzAYE9kqFQLTFeasfAC","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
