_lemma_separator` as it stands (no new statement; a decidable connectivity check is not attempted) | — |","+","+Decidability is supplied so that `decide` can run on a concrete graph:","+adjacency after `contractEdge`, `isolate`, `applyStep` and, by recursion,","+`applySeq` and `minorOf`; `StepValid` and `IsContractionSeq` themselves. The","+`Bool` checker is the item's (iii); on a concrete `SimpleGraph (Fin n)` either","+`checkSeq G seq = true` or `IsContractionSeq G seq` is decided.","+","+### 9.2 State before you prove: the brute-force check, and two statements corrected","+","+`09_lean/check.py` transcribes the Lean definitions on bit masks (`contractEdge`,","+`isolate`, `applySeq`, `closedNbhd`, `degreeIn`, `minDegreeIn`, the `Bool`","+checker) and runs them on **every graph on 1–8 vertices** (nauty-geng, 13,598","+graphs) with the subset-DP vertex separation as the pathwidth oracle:","+","+| statement | checked on | violations |","+|---|---|---|","+| (i) Harper's contrapositive at every level `0 ≤ j ≤ n` (`f(j) − j ≤ pw`) | 120,841 levels | **0** (tight on 8,115 graphs, 59.7%) |","+| (ii) `minDegreeIn (applySeq G seq) S ≤ pw` on random legal sequences, `S` the survivors and a random `S` | 271,960 sequences | **0** |","+| (iii) `checkSeq` agrees with `IsContractionSeq`, legal and illegal | 271,960 + 239,647 (one step retargeted to a non-neighbour) | **0** (no illegal sequence accepted) |","+| removed vertices are isolated in `applySeq`; the minor's pathwidth `≤ pw`; its min degree `≤` its pathwidth | 271,960 | **0** |","+| (v) the Lean minor equals the record's replay (`u` keeps its label, alive set, edges) | 271,960 | **0** |","+","+Two statements the item's text gives are false without a hypothesis, and were","+found so by the check before anything was stated; each is also *proved false*","+in Lean on the one-vertex graph, next to the corrected theorem:","+","+- **(i) needs `j ≤ n`.** For `j = n + 1` no set has size `j`, the premise is","+  vacuous for every `k`, and `k + 1 ≤ pw` fails at `k = pw`","+  (`pathwidth_ge_of_forall_closedNbhd_needs_le`). The SAT certificates of §3","+  always have `1 ≤ t ≤ n` (the checker rejects anything else, line 266 of","+  `obstruction_check.py`), so no certificate on record is affected.","+- **(ii) in the item's degree form needs a nonempty minor.** \"`∀ v ∉ removed seq,","+  d ≤ degree v` in the minor `→ d ≤ pw`\" is vacuous once every vertex is","+  removed — 30,785 of the 271,960 random sequences do — and then claims","+  `pw ≥ d` for any `d` (`pathwidth_ge_of_minor_forall_degree_needs_nonempty`).","+  The stated theorem carries `∃ v, v ∉ removed seq`; the `minDegreeIn` form","+  needs nothing, because `minDegreeIn` of the empty set is `0`.","+","+### 9.3 Three certificates closed by `decide`","+","+| instance | certificate | decided | result |","+|---|---|---|---|","+| `octGraph`, the 8-cycle (pathwidth 2) | contract `7, 6, 5, 4, 3` into `0`: the triangle `{0, 1, 2}` | `checkSeq … = true` and `minDegreeOfMinor … = 2` by `decide` | `two_le_pathwidth_octGraph`: `2 ≤ pathwidth`, tight |","+| `k34 = K_{3,4}` (pathwidth 3) | level `j = 1`: every singleton has `|N[A]| = 4 > 1 + 2` | `∀ A : Finset (Fin 7), A.card = 1 → 1 + 2 < |N[A]|` over all 128 subsets, by `decide` | `three_le_pathwidth_k34`: `3 ≤ pathwidth`, tight |","+| **`Warwick 1729: balanced orders, 3 orders per product`** (Harvey `wbo_30_30`, 30 customers, 81 edges; the one `gap338` instance whose family-M certificate on record has the `bound` status, §4: `ladder.json`, floor 8, optimum 9) | the record's 15 contractions **plus 7 least-c contractions** (below) to an 8-vertex `K₈`, min degree 7 | `checkSeq … = true` and `7 ≤ minDegreeOfMinor …` by `decide +kernel`, **directly on `warwickInstance.mospGraph`, the MOSP graph Lean builds from the instance's 90 requirements** | `seven_le_pathwidth_warwick`; `eight_le_mospValue_warwick`: **every pattern order of `Warwick 1729` opens at least 8 stacks** |","+","+The item expected `decide` to reach toy sizes only. It reaches the record: the","+kernel caches closed terms, so the nested `contractEdge`s cost nothing like the","+`3^k` adjacency queries a naive count predicts. Timings","+(`09_lean/warwick_timings.txt`, one core): the record's 15-step `checkSeq` on","+30 vertices, 1.3 s; the 22-step certificate from the edge list, 2.9 s; the same","+from the matrix through `mospGraph`, 7.8 s; the whole library file, 7.6 s in","+`lake build`. The 100–125-customer certificates of §5 were not tried (outside","+the item; the next size to measure).","+","+**A finding about the record's `bound` certificates.** The C program's `bound`","+status reports `lower = 7` on the 15-vertex minor, and that `lower` is the","+minor's **contraction degeneracy** (MMD+, the C's floor; `cli/README.md`), not","+its minimum degree: the minor's minimum degree is **5** and its degeneracy is","+5 too (`decide +kernel` answers \"`minDegreeOfMinor … = 7` is false\" in 7.3 s,","+and `check.py`'s transcription agrees). So the certificate as written does not","+exhibit the object the theorem needs; the C program found a further","+contraction, to a minor of minimum degree 7, and did not print it. The","+extension is recomputed here by the least-c rule (contract a minimum-degree","+vertex into the neighbour sharing fewest neighbours, `09_lean/warwick_extension.json`,","+7 steps, reaching `K₈`), appended to the record's sequence, and the **whole","+22-step sequence is what Lean checks** — the record's floor 8 is proved from","+the instance's own matrix. The same holds of every `c_status = bound`","+certificate of §4–§5 (39) and of `paper1/dataset.py`'s `minor_certificate`","+(whose `ops` list *is* the contraction sequence to the min-degree minor, so it","+is covered as it stands). **Proposed, not applied**: the C program's `-v` line,","+or the certificate writer, should emit the MMD+ contractions behind a `bound`","+status, so that the theorem applies to the file without recomputation; the","+checker's `theorems` strings now name the new theorems and say so","+(`paper1/obstruction_check.py`, `THEOREMS` and `MINOR_THEOREMS`).","+","+### 9.4 Kill verdict, and what this does not claim","+","+**Kill criterion — met.** \"A statement false on a graph to 8 vertices is","+corrected before it is stated; nothing is stated that is not checked\": two","+statements were corrected before being stated (§9.2), both with their","+counterexample proved in Lean; every stated theorem was checked on all 13,598","+graphs with zero violations; the three `decide`d instances were checked by the","+same script first (`check.py`'s `concrete()`). No stop condition fired: no","+bound above an optimum, no certificate rejected, no false statement committed.","+","+**Deliverables.** `lean/MOSPFormalization/ObstructionCertificate.lean` (22","+theorems); the import in `lean/MOSPFormalization.lean`; 22 `#print axioms`","+lines in `paper1/axiom_check.lean`; `OBSTRUCTION_PROVED` (22 names) in","+`learning/sandwich.py`'s `ALL_PROVED`, with `reports/sandwich_tables.md`","+regenerated (lean stage, then `degree_bound`); `tests/test_obstruction_lean.py`","+(7 tests); the paper's Lean appendix row `obstruction`","+(`paper1/latex/sec9a_appendix_lean.tex`, PDF rebuilt, 77 pages); scratch","+`09_lean/{check.py, run.log, warwick_extension.json, warwick_timings.txt,","+warwick_{check,mindeg,full,mosp}.lean}`.","+","+**Does not claim.** That a C-program *refutation* on a minor or a branch is","+checked in Lean: it rests on `Search/`'s soundness theorems and the binary's","+faithfulness, as before (so `Warwick 1729`'s optimum 9, certified by a","+refutation on a 17-vertex minor, is not a Lean theorem; its floor 8 is). That","+`decide` scales to the 125-customer certificates (not tried). That the","+branch certificate has a decidable form (its connectivity hypotheses are","+`SimpleGraph.Connected` on induced subgraphs; not attempted). That the","+transcription in `check.py` is the Lean definition: it is a transcription,","+checked against the record's replay and the DP, not a proof."]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/home/al/dev/MOSP/reports/obstruction_search.md"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01YG9ar368PFDUnWEBPgkRri","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
