{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011Cgfr5QG2xxsdAEuG728pX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Item 09 is done, marked `[x]`, with PROGRESS.md updated to 9/11 and the gate passing. Two items remain, so no `LOOP_COMPLETE` line.\n\n**What was done.** `lean/MOSPFormalization/ObstructionCertificate.lean` states, in the form the checker cites, that a checked certificate implies the bound: Harper's contrapositive for an UNSAT expansion level (`pathwidth_ge_of_unsat`, `mospValue_ge_of_unsat`), the min-degree minor certificate for the C program's `bound` status (`pathwidth_ge_of_minor_minDegree`, `mospValue_ge_of_minor_minDegree`), and a `Bool` replay `checkSeq` proved sound and complete, with decidable adjacency along a contraction sequence. 22 theorems, no `sorry`, no `axiom`, all on the three standard axioms; imported, axiom-check lines added, folded into `learning/sandwich.py`, a Lean appendix row in the paper, 7 new tests.\n\n**State before you prove paid off.** The brute-force check on all 13,598 graphs to 8 vertices found zero violations, but two of the item's own statements are false without a hypothesis: Harper's contrapositive needs `j ≤ n`, and the degree form of the minor bound needs a nonempty minor. Both were corrected before being stated, and both counterexamples are proved in Lean.\n\n**`decide` reached a record instance.** Beyond the two toy cases, the 30-customer bound-gap instance `Warwick 1729` is closed end to end: `eight_le_mospValue_warwick` proves every pattern order opens at least 8 stacks, decided by `decide +kernel` in 7.6 s on the MOSP graph Lean builds from the instance's own matrix. The item expected toy sizes only.\n\n**One finding about the record.** The C program's `bound` status reports the minor's contraction degeneracy, not its minimum degree (5 on the record's 15-vertex minor, against the reported 7). The filed certificate therefore does not exhibit the object the theorem needs; seven least-c contractions, recomputed, take it to a `K₈`, and that 22-step sequence is what Lean checks. Emitting those steps from the C program is proposed, not applied. Report §9 and PROGRESS.md carry the details, timings and the kill verdict (met)."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1546,"cache_read_input_tokens":262610,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1546,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":774,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"171ae345-0826-42fc-976d-fc244650ed98","uuid":"c27c01b9-307a-47ce-b07c-542267ad58c5","timestamp":"2026-11-03T10:36:11.820Z","request_id":"req_011Cgfr5Pti9ifQ7zRyagARW"}
